From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 02:35:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(status): unify qualified process identities across
 producers [daveey]

F1: one registry process was stamped with launch profile on session rows but served profile on RPC/roster; exact-identity selection counted it twice. Prefer the row profile only where registry scope is missing, retain named route/checkpoint ownership, and exclude recorded foreign profiles from tagged rows.

The real cross-producer test also found same-probe copies conflicting because their request-derived age_seconds differed. Re-project copies at the consumer clock before exact-identity selection; retain actual state/source conflicts and profile separation.

Root (happened): row annotations fell back to launch-global scope while RPCs used served scope. Root (not caught): earlier source/consumer fixtures called the projector directly rather than exercising the real registry, row annotation and dispatcher together. Recurrence: reviewed d6d88ccd420 and earlier producer history 29b07d639a6; this is the first F1 correction.

Proof: tests on d6d88ccd420 fail for default/work identity mismatch, live=2 instead of 1, derived-age conflict, and same-session-id cross-profile qualification. Final canonical run: 60 Python passed; 381 Vitest passed; scripts/check 16 checks passed; renderer tsc passed with 4 GiB heap. Shared executable fixture uses real SQLite, child PID/birth, registry, row annotation, process.list dispatcher and subagent.roster.
